    "created_at": "2026-11-22T17:38:03Z",
    "updated_at": "2026-11-22T17:38:03Z",
    "body": "Preconditions for this slice (S3), from the review of PR #3532 (the kernel of #2627):\n\n1. The kernel was run on the software adapter only. On a hardware adapter the WGSL division and `sqrt` are not always correctly rounded, and a compiler can fuse multiply and add. The estimate is that the error stays under half of the claim margin (4.9e-5). This is not proven. Prove the parity on a hardware adapter before something other than the display reads the buffer.\n2. `adapter.rs:78` takes the software adapter first. In the product the shared device is then WARP, which runs on the CPU. This slice must use the render device or a hardware adapter.\n3. `cut_or_cpu` always takes the GPU when one exists. The ball case is slower on the GPU for a small batch (11.9 ms against 1.1 ms on the fixture). Choose the path by batch size and adapter type, from timings measured on hardware.\n",
    "author_association": "OWNER",
